d) has no test. It is the second place that maps the error to a cause.\n  - file: \"internal/committer/transient_test.go\"\n    severity: low\n    blocking: false\n    message: |\n      plan.md's credential-redaction test (a token in the stderr of a transient failure is redacted in the error and in the committer.retry log) was not written. The log carries cause.Error(), so a test would guard against leaks.\n---\nThe transient-retry change covers the main, code-create and init lanes. It detects a push that landed despite the error, keeps the transient and rejection budgets separate, and the changed packages pass. The previous round's findings are all still present, none of them blocking, so this is approved.\n\n## Checks\n- `go test ./internal/gitx ./internal/committer ./internal/closeout`: all pass.\n- Lint: `make lint` was not re-run. In the previous round `go vet ./...` stopped on a testdata file this change did not touch, and per-package vet of the changed packages was clean.\n- Diff coverage: no per-line report. The new paths have named tests. The worker branch and `github.IsTransientToken` are thinly covered.\n\n## Previous findings\n- internal/closeout/closeout.go (Retry unconditional): still present\n- internal/worker/run.go (no worker test): still present\n- internal/committer/transient_test.go (redaction test): still present\n- internal/committer/committer.go (pending landed check after transient re-fetches): no longer applicable, accepted as a non-blocking tradeoff\n","numLines":41,"startLine":1,"totalLines":41}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_013MQqVnrVveZBfQFyvubm3z","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01A35TapMuCUJ7hKHtay6e9M","type":"tool_result","content":"costs\nlogs\nplan.md\ntriage-engineer.md\ntriage-lead.md\nworker-engineer.md\n# Plan for #357\n\n## Implementation\n\n### Steps\n1. `internal/gitx/gitx.go` (next to `ErrStaleLease`, line ~27): add `ErrTransient = errors.New(\"gitx: transient remote or network failure\")`. New.\n2. `internal/gitx/write.go`: add `classifyTransient(stderr string) bool` (new) matching, case-insensitively: `remote: Internal Server Error`, `The requested URL returned error: 500|502|503|504`, `Could not resolve host`, `Connection reset`, `Operation timed out`, `SSL_read`, `early EOF`, `RPC failed`, `unable to access` combined with `Connection timed out`/`Failed to connect`. In `Push`, after the stale/non-fast-forward cases (those win, so existing behaviour is unchanged), return `fmt.Errorf(\"gitx: push %s: %w\", op.Ref, ErrTransient)` when it matches. Wrap the original error text too (`%w: %v`) so the reason is logged; the text is already scrubbed by `g.run`. Update the doc comment on `Push`.\n3. Token errors: in `Push` (line 67-70) and `fetch` in `internal/gitx/local.go:136-139`, when `op.Token` fails with a network error (`errors.As` to `net.Error`/`*net.OpError`/`*net.DNSError`, `context.DeadlineExceeded` from the client rather than the caller's ctx, or `io.ErrUnexpectedEOF`) or a 5xx, wrap with `ErrTransient` as well as the cause. For the 5xx case, add an exported `github.IsTransient(err error) bool` (new, `internal/github/auth.go`) that unwraps `*github.ErrorResponse` / ghinstallation's `*ghinstallation.HTTPError` status >= 500. gitx must not import github if that creates a cycle, so instead make the check a small `gitx` helper using `interface{ StatusCode() int }`/`net.Error`; the worker verifies which fits the existing import graph.\n4. `internal/gitx/local.go` `classifyFetch`: return `ErrTransient` for the same stderr patterns after the existing `ErrRefNotFound`/`ErrRepoAccess` checks (those win). Do not treat a 403/404 as transient.\n5. `internal/effects/effects.go:33-34`: export `ErrTransient = gitx.ErrTransient` alongside the others.\n6. `internal/committer/errors.go`: add `ErrTransient = errors.New(\"committer: transient remote failure persisted\")`, new; `lane.run` returns an error that wraps both it and the last cause, so callers can match with `errors.Is`.\n7. `internal/committer/committer.go`:\n   - Add `maxTransient = 5` and a `transientBackoff(n int) time.Duration` on `core` (new): 1s,2s,4s,8s,16s with ±25% jitter, total capped about 1 minute. Honour `cfg.Backoff` when set so tests stay fast (tests pass a zero-delay func).\n   - In `lane.attempt` (line 404-406) return a third state. Change the `retry bool` result into a small `retryKind` (none, rejection, transient) or return the error and classify in `run` with `errors.Is(err, effects.ErrTransient)`. The latter is the smaller change: `attempt` keeps `retry=false` for transient and `run` checks the error.\n   - In `lane.run` (line 251-291) keep two counters: `pushes` (rejections, `maxPushes`) and `transients` (`maxTransient`), independent. On a transient error from `fetch` or from `attempt`: `reset`, log `committer.retry` at `InfoContext` with `\"reason\", \"transient\"`, branch, attempt and the (scrubbed) `err`, sleep `transientBackoff`, loop again. Do not set `prev = base` for the lease-conflict check unless the push was rejected; a transient retry re-fetches, so a landed push is seen.\n   - Landed-push detection: after the re-fetch, if the push that failed transiently created commit `sha` (record it from `cr.SHA` in `attempt`, returned in `Result.SHA` alongside the error) and the new `base == sha`, or `git merge-base --is-ancestor sha base` (use existing `l.g` helpers, add a gitx method if none exists), return `Result{SHA: sha}` as success with no second commit. Also covers the case where the snapshot re-applied on the new base yields no staged change: `attempt` already returns `NoOp`, which is a success.\n   - Exhaustion: return the error wrapping `ErrTransient` (`%w`), `Attempts` set.\n   - Do not retry when `create` is true and the push is transient *and* the branch already exists with a different SHA: the existing `ErrBranchExists` path in `attempt` (line 401) is for rejections only, a transient error on `create` is retried via `run`'s caller in `code.go:244 create`. Add the same loop around `l.attempt(ctx, s, s.base, true)` in `internal/committer/code.go:260`. After a transient failure, fetch the branch; if it exists at the pushed SHA return success, otherwise retry. If it exists at another SHA keep `ErrBranchExists`.\n8. `internal/committer/init.go:208-215`: wrap the init push in the same bounded transient retry; if `ard-init` now exists at the pushed commit return success, otherwise keep `ErrInitExists` for rejections. Share the backoff helper from step 7.\n9. Close-out cause. No existing cause names this: `CauseCloneFail` is specific to clone, `CauseRateLimit` to the agent's API errors. Add `CausePushTransient CauseKind = \"push_transient\"` (new, `internal/closeout/closeout.go:104`) and mention it in `internal/reaper/doc.go:51`. In `Closer.commit` (`internal/closeout/closeout.go:~620`), before the `failedPlan` fallback, add: `if errors.Is(err, committer.ErrTransient)` then set `rec.Job.Cause = Cause{Kind: CausePushTransient, Detail: \"remote unavailable after retries\", Transient: true, Retry: <job is not itself a retry>}` and `*p = retryPlan(rec.Job, \"push_transient: ...\")`, keeping Tail/TailWithheld/KeepUntil like the other branches. Use the same `Retry` rule as `reaper.NewCause` (`internal/reaper/finish.go:73`, `RetryOf == \"\"`): confirm the `closeout.Job` has a field for it, otherwise pass it through `Job`. When the job is itself a retry, `Retry` is false and the plan still must not be `ard:executor:failed`: this needs a check against `prepare.go:225-229`, which maps `Cause.Retry` false to `failedPlan`. If so, use `limitedPlan`-like handling or leave the job failed and say so in the comment; flag it to the reviewer.\n10. `internal/worker/run.go:628-640`: when `CommitCode` returns `committer.ErrTransient`, finish with `closeout.CausePushTransient`, transient true and `!jb.pushed` retry, instead of `CauseNoProcess` (line 641).\n11. GH006 comment: out of scope for this change. It changes the meaning of a protection failure and needs a policy decision (retry count, needs-human wording). It should be a separate issue. Do not classify `GH006` as transient here.\n\n### Test plan\nCommand: `go test ./internal/gitx/... ./internal/committer/... ./internal/closeout/... ./internal/worker/...` then `go test ./...`.\n- `internal/gitx/gitx_test.go` `TestPushTransientClassification` (table): stderr `remote: Internal Server Error`, `The requested URL returned error: 502`, `Could not resolve host: github.com`, `Connection reset by peer`, `early EOF`, `RPC failed` each give `ErrTransient`; `stale info` stays `ErrStaleLease`; `non-fast-forward` stays `ErrNonFastForward`; `error: 403` is not transient. Use a fake `git` on PATH or the existing runner seam.\n- `TestFetchTransient`: same patterns on `FetchRef`; `couldn't find remote ref` stays `ErrRefNotFound`.\n- Token failure: a `TokenFunc` returning a `*net.DNSError` gives `ErrTransient`; a plain error does not.\n- `internal/committer/committer_test.go` `TestTransientRetry`: fake pushes 500 once, then accepts. Expect the commit on the remote, `Attempts` 2, one `committer.retry` log record with reason `transient`, no error.\n- `TestTransientPushLanded`: the first push is applied to the remote and then reports a 500. Expect success, the remote has exactly one new commit, `Result.SHA` is that commit.\n- `TestTransientExhausted`: always 500. Expect `errors.Is(err, ErrTransient)` after `maxTransient` tries, and a rejection counter that is independent (a mix of one stale lease and transients still gets its full budgets).\n- `TestRejectionUnchanged`: the existing table in `committer_test.go:187` passes untouched.\n- Code lane and init lane: one transient-then-success case each; the code lane `create` case where the branch landed returns success, not `ErrBranchExists`.\n- `internal/closeout/closer_test.go`: commit returns `ErrTransient` gives `OutcomeRetry`, cause `push_transient`, no `ard:executor:failed`; a job that is itself a retry has the expected plan. A non-transient commit error still gives `failedPlan`.\n- Credential redaction: a token appearing in the stderr of a transient failure is `[REDACTED]` in the error and in the `committer.retry` log.\n- Edge cases: ctx cancelled during the backoff returns `ctx.Err()`, not `ErrTransient`; jitter stays within the cap.\n\n### Risk\nMedium. The retry loop in `lane.run` is shared by every commit lane and handles the case where a push may have landed, so a mistake could write a duplicate or lose a commit. Security-sensitive: error text goes to logs, so the existing scrubbing must stay in place. It adds a close-out cause and changes how a commit failure maps to a plan, which the Reaper sees. No protected paths in `merge.protected_paths` are touched. No public CLI or migration changes. Concurrency: the lane semaphore is held during backoff (up to about 1 minute), which delays other requests on the same branch.\n\n### Size\nM to L (roughly 250 to 450 changed lines including tests). Files: `internal/gitx/gitx.go`, `write.go`, `local.go`, `gitx_test.go`; `internal/effects/effects.go`; `internal/committer/errors.go`, `committer.go`, `code.go`, `init.go`, `committer_test.go`; `internal/closeout/closeout.go`, `closer_test.go`; `internal/worker/run.go`; `internal/reaper/doc.go`.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d3c737a2-b58b-4ad1-b9b2-df621e9e8705","uuid":"8e686ac6-fbc6-44d4-9f20-3444a87a7682","timestamp":"2026-11-25T14:57:15.699Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"costs\nlogs\nplan.md\ntriage-engineer.md\ntriage-lead.md\nworker-engineer.md\n# Plan for #357\n\n## Implementation\n\n### Steps\n1. `internal/gitx/gitx.go` (next to `ErrStaleLease`, line ~27): add `ErrTransient = errors.New(\"gitx: transient remote or network failure\")`. New.\n2. `internal/gitx/write.go`: add `classifyTransient(stderr string) bool` (new) matching, case-insensitively: `remote: Internal Server Error`, `The requested URL returned error: 500|502|503|504`, `Could not resolve host`, `Connection reset`, `Operation timed out`, `SSL_read`, `early EOF`, `RPC failed`, `unable to access` combined with `Connection timed out`/`Failed to connect`. In `Push`, after the stale/non-fast-forward cases (those win, so existing behaviour is unchanged), return `fmt.Errorf(\"gitx: push %s: %w\", op.Ref, ErrTransient)` when it matches. Wrap the original error text too (`%w: %v`) so the reason is logged; the text is already scrubbed by `g.run`. Update the doc comment on `Push`.\n3. Token errors: in `Push` (line 67-70) and `fetch` in `internal/gitx/local.go:136-139`, when `op.Token` fails with a network error (`errors.As` to `net.Error`/`*net.OpError`/`*net.DNSError`, `context.DeadlineExceeded` from the client rather than the caller's ctx, or `io.ErrUnexpectedEOF`) or a 5xx, wrap with `ErrTransient` as well as the cause. For the 5xx case, add an exported `github.IsTransient(err error) bool` (new, `internal/github/auth.go`) that unwraps `*github.ErrorResponse` / ghinstallation's `*ghinstallation.HTTPError` status >= 500. gitx must not import github if that creates a cycle, so instead make the check a small `gitx` helper using `interface{ StatusCode() int }`/`net.Error`; the worker verifies which fits the existing import graph.\n4. `internal/gitx/local.go` `classifyFetch`: return `ErrTransient` for the same stderr patterns after the existing `ErrRefNotFound`/`ErrRepoAccess` checks (those win). Do not treat a 403/404 as transient.\n5. `internal/effects/effects.go:33-34`: export `ErrTransient = gitx.ErrTransient` alongside the others.\n6. `internal/c